UID:connect-and-create-professional-mobilities-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T204057Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260701
SUMMARY:Deadline: Connect and Create: Professional Mobilities for Performin
 g Arts (Africa-Europe) - 30 June 2026 Cut-Off
DESCRIPTION:Connect and Create Professional Mobilities call supports organi
 sations and international events in Africa or Europe to host delegations o
 f NON-ARTIST performing arts professionals from both continents. Part of t
 he Africa-Europe Partnerships for Culture programme (EUR 8M\, implemented 
 by the Goethe-Institut and Expertise France with Institut francais). HOSTI
 NG CONTEXTS: festivals\, biennials and major international events\; fairs\
 , markets and conventions\; summits\, seminars\, symposiums and workshops.
  DELEGATES MAY INCLUDE: event organisers\; programmers\, producers and age
 nts\; network managers\; representatives of companies and festivals\; tech
 nical\, communications and PR managers. DELEGATION COMPOSITION: at least 8
  cultural professionals (18+) from one of the 48 sub-Saharan African count
 ries or one of the 27 EU countries\; strong international dimension requir
 ed (5+ different nationalities for delegations of 8-10\, or 8+ nationaliti
 es for delegations larger than 10). APPLICANT ELIGIBILITY: associations\, 
 foundations\, cultural institutions\, private companies\, etc. with proven
  experience in performing arts\, based in one of the 48 sub-Saharan Africa
 n countries or the 27 EU Member States. INDIVIDUALS CANNOT APPLY. SELECTIO
 N: two committees (January and September 2026). DEADLINE: this card is for
  the 30 June 2026 cut-off (the earlier 30 November 2025 cut-off has passed
 ). APPLY via the Institut francais emundus portal.\n\nOrganisation: Goethe
 -Institut and Expertise France\, in collaboration with Institut francais (
 Africa-Europe Partnerships for Culture consortium)\nLocation: Hosting even
 ts in one of the 48 Sub-Saharan African countries or one of the 27 EU Memb
 er States\nAward: EUR 15\,000 to EUR 25\,000 per hosting organisation\, co
 vering travel\, visa and insurance costs for delegation members. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: Mobility hosting between March 2026 and December 202
 7\n\nMore: https://ifprog.emundus.fr/en/campagne-info?view=programme&cid=3
 11&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ifprog.emundus.fr/en/campagne-info?view=programme&cid=311&utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hosting events in one of the 48 Sub-Saharan African countries or o
 ne of the 27 EU Member States
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:connect-and-create-circulation-performing-arts-music-2026@artificialnou
 veau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T204057Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Connect and Create: Circulation of Performing Arts and Mu
 sic (Africa-Europe) - 2nd Call
DESCRIPTION:The Circulation strand of Connect and Create funds the touring 
 and dissemination of African artistic creations across Africa and Europe. 
 It is part of the Africa-Europe Partnerships for Culture programme (EUR 8M
 \, led by the Goethe-Institut and Expertise France in partnership with Ins
 titut francais\, supported by the European Union)\, and is a different str
 and from the Professional Mobilities call also on the desk. THIS CARD IS T
 HE SECOND CALL\, deadline 30 September 2026 (the first call closed 30 Nove
 mber 2025). AMOUNT: EUR 15\,000 to EUR 39\,500 per project. WHAT IS FUNDED
 : mobility costs for artistic teams\, including transport\, visas\, insura
 nce\, lodging\, per diems\, local transport\, and shipping of scenographic
  and technical elements. WHO CAN APPLY: artistic teams (performing arts co
 mpanies\, music ensembles\, collectives) based in sub-Saharan Africa\; dis
 semination structures (production houses\, artist managers\, theatres\, la
 bels\, venues) based in Africa or Europe\; and event organisers (festivals
 \, markets\, professional gatherings) in Africa or Europe. Applicants must
  be legally established in one of the 47 eligible sub-Saharan African coun
 tries\, Kenya among them\, or one of the 27 EU Member States. INDIVIDUALS 
 CANNOT APPLY. ELIGIBLE PROJECTS\, two formats: (1) TOURS\, requiring a min
 imum of 5 pre-booked dates across at least 3 different African countries\,
  or at least 3 pre-booked dates in one or more European countries\; (2) PR
 OGRAMMING WITHIN MAJOR EVENTS\, requiring a festival\, market or professio
 nal gathering in Africa or Europe to host at least 3 artistic teams from d
 ifferent African countries. TIMELINE: activities must take place between F
 ebruary and December 2027\; selection committee December 2026\, results an
 nounced January 2027. PRIORITY is given to projects that build on existing
  tandems already collaborating\, feature emerging artists\, use eco-respon
 sible practices\, and address inclusion. APPLY via the Institut francais e
 mundus portal. Questions: connectandcreate@expertisefrance.fr.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Goethe-Institut and Expertise France\, in collaboration with Institu
 t francais (Africa-Europe Partnerships for Culture consortium)\nLocation: 
 Applicants based in one of the 47 eligible sub-Saharan African countries (
 Kenya included) or one of the 27 EU Member States. Touring in Africa and/o
 r Europe.\nAward: EUR 15\,000 to EUR 39\,500 per project\, covering travel
 \, visas\, insurance\, accommodation\, per diems\, local transport and shi
 pping of scenographic and technical elements. No application fee.\nDuratio
 n: Projects carried out between February and December 2027\n\nMore: https:
 //ifprog.emundus.fr/en/campagne-info?view=programme&cid=353&utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ifprog.emundus.fr/en/campagne-info?view=programme&cid=353&utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicants based in one of the 47 eligible sub-Saharan African cou
 ntries (Kenya included) or one of the 27 EU Member States. Touring in Afri
 ca and/or Europe.
END:VEVENT
